.TH BRIGHTNESS 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manuals"
.SH NAME
brightness \- adjust display backlight brightness using brightnessctl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brightness
[\fIOPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brightness
is a simple wrapper script that provides a standardized interface to the
.MR brightnessctl 1
utility. It allows users to query, increase, or decrease the display brightness 
level in fixed increments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-get
Retrieve the current brightness level as a percentage (0-100).
.TP
.B \-\-inc
Increase the current brightness by a fixed step of 5%.
.TP
.B \-\-dec
Decrease the current brightness by a fixed step of 5%.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display the help menu and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B brightness \-\-inc
Increase the display brightness by 5%.
.TP
.B brightness \-\-get
Output the current brightness percentage to standard output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The script relies on the presence of the
.MR brightnessctl 1
command in the system's PATH.
.SH BUGS
Brightness levels are capped between 5% and 100%. The script prevents setting 
the brightness to 0% to avoid accidentally rendering the display unusable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR brightnessctl 1 ,
.MR cut 1
